HST: mail-merge results get no automatic blank pages where a recipient restarts the page numbering

Each recipient of a merged document starts on a new page with the page number restarted at 1
(Word writes pgNumType start=1 the same way). Writer treats an odd page number as a right page and
inserts an automatic blank page when it would land on a left page, so three letters became five
pages, and five printed sheets. Word keeps the page where it is.

Documents produced by the HST mail merge carry the user-defined document property HSTMergeResult;
for them, the side of a page that restarts the numbering follows its position, as in Word. A page
style that is left-only or right-only still decides the side. Every other document keeps Writer's
rule. The decision is in sw/source/core/layout/hst/hstmergeresultlayout (HST-owned); the four
layout places that read the side from a page number ask it.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_hst_merge_result_pages.

